whisper: Physics for boxes. Use: use: physics.fathom  x, y is the top left; speeds are per second.

a body has:
  x (a number)
  y (a number)
  width (a number)
  height (a number)
  speed across (a number)
  speed down (a number)
  bounciness (a number)
  fixed (yes or no)
  landed (yes or no)
and the universe said i love you

a physics world has:
  bodies (a list of bodies)
  gravity (a number)
and the universe said i love you

to a box at, given x (a number) and y (a number) and width (a number) and height (a number), returning a body:
  set b to conjure a body
  set the x of b to x
  set the y of b to y
  set the width of b to width
  set the height of b to height
  return b
and the universe said i love you

to a wall at, given x (a number) and y (a number) and width (a number) and height (a number), returning a body:
  set b to a box at with (x, y, width, height)
  set the fixed of b to yes
  return b
and the universe said i love you

to touching, given first (a body) and second (a body), returning yes or no:
  if the x of first is at least the x of second plus the width of second:
    return no
  if the x of first plus the width of first is at most the x of second:
    return no
  if the y of first is at least the y of second plus the height of second:
    return no
  return the y of first plus the height of first exceeds the y of second
and the universe said i love you

to include the body, for a physics world, given b (a body):
  add b to bodies
and the universe said i love you

to the body numbered, for a physics world, given which (a number), returning a body:
  return item which of bodies
and the universe said i love you

to change the body, for a physics world, given which (a number) and b (a body):
  set item which of bodies to b
and the universe said i love you

to push the body, for a physics world, given which (a number) and across (a number) and down (a number):
  set b to item which of bodies
  set the speed across of b to across
  set the speed down of b to down
  set item which of bodies to b
and the universe said i love you

whisper: Each body falls, then moves across, then down, stopped by what it hits.
to step the physics, for a physics world, given seconds (a number):
  for each k from 1 to the size of bodies:
    set b to item k of bodies
    if not the fixed of b:
      set the speed down of b to the speed down of b plus gravity times seconds
      set the x of b to the x of b plus the speed across of b times seconds
      for each j from 1 to the size of bodies:
        set other to item j of bodies
        if j is not k and touching with (b, other):
          if the speed across of b exceeds 0:
            set the x of b to the x of other minus the width of b
          otherwise:
            set the x of b to the x of other plus the width of other
          set the speed across of b to 0 minus the speed across of b times the bounciness of b
      set the landed of b to no
      set the y of b to the y of b plus the speed down of b times seconds
      for each j from 1 to the size of bodies:
        set other to item j of bodies
        if j is not k and touching with (b, other):
          if the speed down of b exceeds 0:
            set the y of b to the y of other minus the height of b
            set the landed of b to yes
          otherwise:
            set the y of b to the y of other plus the height of other
          set the speed down of b to 0 minus the speed down of b times the bounciness of b
      set item k of bodies to b
and the universe said i love you
